md`# brain-library

Notebooks kept by a Cloud Brain and served from its address. The files are in \`brain-static\`, under \`library/\`; this Worker keeps the list, the versions and who may open each.

| | |
|---|---|
| Worker | \`brain-x-library\` |
| \`library.put\` | procedure, the owner's own session; a token or a turn is refused, because the file is served as a page. \`?name=\`, optional \`public=true\` and \`parent=<sha256>\`; the body is the notebook's HTML file. |
| \`library.list\` | query, anyone. The owner gets every notebook, anyone else the public ones; a member granted the method is anyone else. |
| \`library.versions\` | query, owner. \`?name=\`. The last 10 saves, newest first. |
| \`library.setPublic\` | procedure, owner. \`{ name, public }\` |
| \`library.delete\` | procedure, owner. \`{ name }\`. Deletes every version. |
| \`library.index\` | procedure, owner. \`{ name }\`. Enters the module cards of the newest version again (see Module cards). \`{ name, cards }\`. |
| \`GET /library/<name>\` | the notebook. Anyone for a public one, the owner for any. \`?v=<sha256>\` opens a kept version. |
| Calls | \`static.put\`, \`static.get\`, \`static.delete\`, \`knowledge.put\` |
| Storage | \`rows\`, key \`n/<name>\`: \`{ title, sha256, size, public, savedAt, versions }\`. Files at \`library/<name>/<first 16 of sha256>.html\` in \`brain-static\`. |

A name is 1 to 80 of \`A-Z a-z 0-9 @ . _ -\`. The body must be a lopecode notebook: a file with a \`bootconf.json\` block. The title is the file's \`<title>\`. With \`parent\`, a put is refused with 409 unless \`parent\` is the SHA-256 of the notebook's newest version (empty for a new name), so two tabs saving one notebook do not overwrite each other unseen.

\`\`\`js
client = xrpcClient("https://brain.example", { namespace: "com.lopecode.brain" })
await client.procedure("library.put", htmlBytes, { params: { name: "notes", public: "true" }, raw: true })
// https://brain.example/library/notes
\`\`\`

\`libraryPanel({ client, origin, owner })\` is the list as a table, with upload, public and delete for the owner.

A notebook served from \`/library\` runs on the Brain's own address, so its cells call the Brain as whoever is signed in. Put only notebooks you would run as yourself.

## Module cards

A put enters one entry in \`brain-x-knowledge\` for each module in the file, of kind \`module\`, so that \`knowledge.search?semantic=true&kind=module\` finds the module for a task (added 2026-10-10). A card is \`libraryCards\`' reading of the module's block: its name and heading as the title; the first prose cell that says something once its headings are removed, the names of its cells (tests and the halves of a \`viewof\` left out) and the modules it imports as the text. Not its source. The card's \`url\` is the notebook's address here and its \`file\` the kept file.

- A module has one card, \`module:<user>:<name>\`, whichever notebook it is in. The last put of a public notebook that has it writes it; while no public notebook has it, the last put of any notebook does.
- The file is read block by block from the top, and a block is a module when it is named \`@user/name\` and is JavaScript that is not encoded. Of the 100 modules \`lope-reader\` lists in the Cloud Brain notebook on 2026-10-10, 96 have a card. The four without are named another way: \`es-module-shims@2.6.2\`, \`@observablehq/runtime@6.0.0\`, \`@observablehq/inspector@5.0.1\` and the Observable id \`d/57d79353bac56631\`. 71 of 75 in \`quick_start\`, the same four left out.
- The cards of a public notebook are public, and say what that notebook's copy of the module says. A put of a notebook that is not public sends its cards with \`unlessPublic\`: \`brain-x-knowledge\` leaves a card that is public whole (its words and its address stay those of the public notebook) and enters the others private. Until 2026-10-10 10:00 CEST such a put kept the card public and wrote the private copy's words and address into it.
- A module that is in a private notebook only, then in a public one: the put of the public notebook makes its card public, with the public copy's words. Nothing makes it private again but a put of \`{ id, public: false }\`.
- A module whose prose is headings alone has a card of its cell names: 3 of the 99 cards on cb4 (\`bootloader\`, \`observable-runtime-v6\`, \`blank-notebook\`). Reading the first prose cell alone left 16 of 100 so, until 2026-10-10.
- \`library.setPublic\` and \`library.delete\` do not change a card. To make one private, put \`{ id, public: false }\` to \`knowledge.put\`; to remove one, \`knowledge.delete\`.
- The put answers \`cards\`, how many were entered; a card left as it was is not counted. When \`knowledge.put\` fails the notebook is kept all the same and \`cards\` is smaller; \`library.index\` enters them again.`
// %%
library_service = cloudflare.Service("library", libraryApp, {
  methods: {
    // A saved notebook is served as a page that runs as whoever opens it: only the owner's own tab saves one, not a token or a turn.
    // Fixed: this Worker is a writer brain-static trusts, so what reaches put is served as a page.
    "com.lopecode.brain.library.put": { type: "procedure", who: "owner", allow: "caller.session", fixed: true },
    "com.lopecode.brain.library.list": { type: "query", who: "anyone" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.library.versions": { type: "query", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.library.setPublic": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.library.delete": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" },
    "com.lopecode.brain.library.index": { type: "procedure", who: "owner" }
  },
  paths: [{ path: "/library/*", who: "anyone" }],
  calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.static.put", "com.lopecode.brain.static.get", "com.lopecode.brain.static.delete", "com.lopecode.brain.knowledge.put"]
})
// %%
library_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", library_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced library_service";
}
// %%
// One card for each module block of a notebook's file: what is read to choose a module, and not its source. The block
// is the text the exporter writes, so the cells are read from its define calls and the prose from its md cells.
libraryCards = (html, { name, file, host, open = false }) => {
  // The tag's name is joined here: written whole in a module, it would end the block the module is kept in.
  const OPEN = "<scr" + "ipt", CLOSE = "</scr" + "ipt>", modules = [];
  // Block by block from the top, as a browser reads the file. A tag written in another block's text starts nothing:
  // a regex over the whole file made a card for "@user/module-name", a line of prose in a wiki page (2026-10-10).
  for (let i = 0; ; ) {
    const at = html.indexOf(OPEN, i), gt = at < 0 ? -1 : html.indexOf(">", at);
    if (gt < 0) break;
    const close = html.indexOf(CLOSE, gt), end = close < 0 ? html.length : close;
    const m = /^\S+\s+id="(@[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+)"\s+type="text\/plain"\s+data-mime="application\/javascript"\s*>$/.exec(html.slice(at, gt + 1));
    if (m) modules.push([m[1], html.slice(gt + 1, end)]);
    i = end + CLOSE.length;
  }
  return modules.map(([module, source]) => {
    const prose = [...source.matchAll(/\{\s*return\s*\(\s*md`((?:[^`\\]|\\[\s\S])*)`/g)].map((p) => p[1].replace(/\\([`\\$])/g, "$1"));
    const heading = (prose.join("\n").match(/^#\s+(.+)$/m) || [])[1];
    const cells = [...new Set([...source.matchAll(/\$def\("[^"]*", "([^"]+)"|\.variable\(observer\("([^"]+)"\)\)/g)].map((d) => d[1] || d[2]))].filter((n) => !/^(test_|viewof |mutable |initial )/.test(n));
    const imports = [...new Set([...source.matchAll(/"module (@[^"]+)"/g)].map((d) => d[1]))];
    // The first prose cell that says something once its headings are gone: many modules open with a cell that is the heading alone.
    const first = prose.map((p) => p.replace(/^#+\s+.+$/gm, "").replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim()).find(Boolean) || "";
    return {
      id: ("module:" + module.slice(1).toLowerCase().replace("/", ":").replace(/[^a-z0-9._:-]/g, "-")).slice(0, 100),
      kind: "module",
      title: (module + (heading ? ": " + heading.trim() : "")).slice(0, 500),
      text: [first.slice(0, 900), cells.length ? "Cells: " + cells.slice(0, 60).join(", ") : "", imports.length ? "Imports: " + imports.join(", ") : ""].filter(Boolean).join("\n").slice(0, 4000),
      url: `https://${host}/library/${name}`,
      source: "library",
      file,
      method: "library.put",
      // A notebook that is not public leaves a card anyone reads as it is.
      ...(open ? { public: true } : { unlessPublic: true })
    };
  });
}
// %%
libraryApp = {
  const app = new hono.Hono();
  const NS = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.library.";
  const STATIC = "com.lopecode.brain.static.";
  const KEEP = 10;
  const fail = (c, status, error, message) => c.json({ error, message }, status);
  const okName = (n) => /^[A-Za-z0-9@._-]{1,80}$/.test(n || "") && !/^\.+$/.test(n);
  // A token is the owner's. A person is not, whatever method they were granted.
  const isOwner = (c) => {
    const who = c.req.header("x-brain-caller") || "";
    return who === "owner" || who.startsWith("token:");
  };
  const fileOf = (name, sha) => `library/${name}/${sha.slice(0, 16)}.html`;
  const drop = (name, sha) => xrpc.fetch(STATIC + "delete", { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify({ path: fileOf(name, sha) }) });
  // The module cards of a file, entered in the knowledge base 100 to a call. Answers how many were entered; a call
  // that fails is not a reason to lose the notebook.
  const enter = async (name, html, head) => {
    const cards = libraryCards(html, { name, file: fileOf(name, head.sha256), host: config.host, open: head.public });
    let entered = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < cards.length; i += 100) {
      const r = await xrpc.fetch("com.lopecode.brain.knowledge.put", { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify({ entries: cards.slice(i, i + 100) }) }).catch(() => null);
      if (r && r.ok) entered += ((await r.json().catch(() => null)) || { ids: [] }).ids.length;
    }
    return entered;
  };
  app.post(NS + "put", async (c) => {
    const name = c.req.query("name") || "";
    if (!okName(name)) return fail(c, 400, "InvalidRequest", "name");
    const bytes = new Uint8Array(await c.req.raw.arrayBuffer());
    const html = new TextDecoder().decode(bytes);
    if (!html.includes('id="bootconf.json"')) return fail(c, 400, "NotANotebook", "the file has no bootconf.json block");
    const head = await rows.get("n/" + name);
    const parent = c.req.query("parent");
    if (parent != null && parent !== (head ? head.sha256 : "")) return fail(c, 409, "StaleParent", `the newest version of ${name} is ${head ? head.sha256 : "none"}`);
    const sha256 = [...new Uint8Array(await crypto.subtle.digest("SHA-256", bytes))].map((b) => b.toString(16).padStart(2, "0")).join("");
    const kept = await xrpc.fetch(STATIC + "put", { method: "POST", params: { path: fileOf(name, sha256), type: "text/html; charset=utf-8", public: "false" }, body: bytes });
    if (!kept.ok) return fail(c, 502, "UpstreamFailed", `static.put answered ${kept.status}`);
    const title = ((html.slice(0, 65536).match(/<title>([^<]*)<\/title>/) || [])[1] || name).trim().slice(0, 200);
    const savedAt = Date.now();
    const versions = [{ sha256, size: bytes.length, savedAt }, ...(head ? head.versions.filter((v) => v.sha256 !== sha256) : [])];
    for (const old of versions.slice(KEEP)) await drop(name, old.sha256);
    const open = c.req.query("public");
    const next = { title, sha256, size: bytes.length, public: open != null ? open === "true" : !!(head && head.public), savedAt, versions: versions.slice(0, KEEP) };
    await rows.put("n/" + name, next);
    return c.json({ name, title, sha256, size: next.size, public: next.public, savedAt, versions: next.versions.length, cards: await enter(name, html, next) });
  });
  app.post(NS + "index", async (c) => {
    const { name } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    const head = okName(name) ? await rows.get("n/" + name) : null;
    if (!head) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", String(name));
    const file = await xrpc.fetch(STATIC + "get", { params: { path: fileOf(name, head.sha256) } });
    if (!file.ok) return fail(c, 502, "UpstreamFailed", `static.get answered ${file.status}`);
    return c.json({ name, cards: await enter(name, await file.text(), head) });
  });
  app.get(NS + "list", async (c) => {
    const all = (await rows.list("n/")).map(({ key, value }) => ({ name: key.slice(2), title: value.title, sha256: value.sha256, size: value.size, public: value.public, savedAt: value.savedAt, versions: value.versions.length }));
    return c.json({ notebooks: isOwner(c) ? all : all.filter((n) => n.public) });
  });
  app.get(NS + "versions", async (c) => {
    const head = await rows.get("n/" + (c.req.query("name") || ""));
    return head ? c.json({ versions: head.versions }) : fail(c, 404, "NotFound", c.req.query("name") || "");
  });
  app.post(NS + "setPublic", async (c) => {
    const { name, public: open } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    const head = okName(name) ? await rows.get("n/" + name) : null;
    if (!head) return fail(c, 404, "NotFound", String(name));
    await rows.put("n/" + name, { ...head, public: !!open });
    return c.json({ name, public: !!open });
  });
  app.post(NS + "delete", async (c) => {
    const { name } = await c.req.json().catch(() => ({}));
    const head = okName(name) ? await rows.get("n/" + name) : null;
    if (!head) return c.json({ deleted: false });
    for (const v of head.versions) await drop(name, v.sha256);
    await rows.delete("n/" + name);
    return c.json({ deleted: true, versions: head.versions.length });
  });
  app.get("/library/:name{.+}", async (c) => {
    const name = c.req.param("name");
    const head = okName(name) ? await rows.get("n/" + name) : null;
    if (!head) return c.text("not found", 404);
    if (!head.public && !isOwner(c)) return c.text("unauthorized", 401);
    const sha = c.req.query("v") || head.sha256;
    if (!head.versions.some((v) => v.sha256 === sha)) return c.text("not found", 404);
    // A caller inside the Brain sees this. workers.dev removes it from a response it may compress (measured 2026-10-06).
    const etag = 'W/"' + sha + '"';
    const headers = { "content-type": "text/html; charset=utf-8", "cache-control": "no-cache", etag, "x-library-sha256": sha };
    if ((c.req.header("if-none-match") || "").includes('"' + sha + '"')) return new Response(null, { status: 304, headers });
    const file = await xrpc.fetch(STATIC + "get", { params: { path: fileOf(name, sha) } });
    return file.ok ? new Response(file.body, { headers }) : c.text("not found", 404);
  });
  return app;
}
// %%
// The list as a table. For the owner: upload a file, make public or private, delete, and save `current` ({ name, html() }).
libraryPanel = ({ client, origin, owner = false, current = null } = {}) => {
  if (!client) return htl.html`<i style="color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)">Open this notebook from a Brain to see its library.</i>`;
  const box = htl.html`<div></div>`, note = htl.html`<div style="color:var(--theme-foreground-muted);margin-top:6px"></div>`;
  let table = null;
  const say = (text) => void (note.textContent = text);
  const draw = async () => {
    const { notebooks } = await client.query("library.list");
    table = Inputs.table(
      notebooks.map((n) => ({ name: n.name, title: n.title, KB: Math.round(n.size / 1024), saved: new Date(n.savedAt), public: n.public, versions: n.versions })),
      {
        multiple: false,
        required: false,
        layout: "auto",
        format: {
          // A link carries no session: a notebook that is not public is fetched with it and opened from the bytes.
          name: (name) =>
            htl.html`<a href=${origin + "/library/" + name} target="_blank" onclick=${async (e) => {
              if (notebooks.find((n) => n.name === name).public || !client.fetch) return;
              e.preventDefault();
              const r = await client.fetch("/library/" + name);
              if (!r.ok) return say(`${name}: ${r.status}`);
              open(URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([await r.arrayBuffer()], { type: "text/html" })), "_blank");
            }}>${name}</a>`,
          saved: (d) => d.toISOString().slice(0, 16).replace("T", " "),
          public: (p) => (p ? "public" : "owner")
        }
      }
    );
    box.replaceChildren(notebooks.length ? table : htl.html`<i style="color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)">No notebooks.</i>`);
  };
  const run = (what, fn) => async () => {
    try {
      say(what + "…");
      say((await fn()) || "");
      await draw();
    } catch (e) {
      say(`${what} failed: ${(e && e.message) || e}`);
    }
  };
  const picked = () => {
    const row = table && table.value;
    if (!row) throw new Error("choose a row");
    return row;
  };
  draw().catch((e) => say("library.list failed: " + ((e && e.message) || e)));
  const refresh = Inputs.button("Refresh", { reduce: run("Refresh", async () => "") });
  if (!owner) return htl.html`<div>${box}${refresh}${note}</div>`;
  const file = Inputs.file({ label: "Notebook file", accept: ".html" });
  const name = Inputs.text({ label: "Name", placeholder: "from the file's name", width: "20em" });
  const put = async (as, bytes) => {
    const made = await client.procedure("library.put", bytes, { params: { name: as }, raw: true });
    return `${made.name} saved, ${made.versions} version${made.versions === 1 ? "" : "s"}: ${origin}/library/${made.name}`;
  };
  const upload = Inputs.button("Upload", {
    reduce: run("Upload", async () => {
      if (!file.value) throw new Error("choose a file");
      return put(name.value || file.value.name.replace(/\.html?$/i, "").replace(/[^A-Za-z0-9@._-]+/g, "-"), new Uint8Array(await file.value.arrayBuffer()));
    })
  });
  const flip = Inputs.button("Make public / owner only", { reduce: run("Change", async () => void (await client.procedure("library.setPublic", { name: picked().name, public: !picked().public }))) });
  const del = Inputs.button("Delete", { reduce: run("Delete", async () => void (await client.procedure("library.delete", { name: picked().name }))) });
  const save = current ? Inputs.button(`Save this notebook as "${current.name}"`, { reduce: run("Save", async () => put(current.name, new TextEncoder().encode(await current.html()))) }) : "";
  return htl.html`<div>${box}<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:8px 0">${refresh}${flip}${del}${save}</div>${file}${name}${upload}${note}</div>`;
}
// %%
md`## Tests`
// %%
libraryNotebook = (body, title = "Notes") => "<html><head><title>" + title + "</title><script id=\"bootconf.json\" type=\"text/plain\">{}</scr" + "ipt></head><body>" + body + "</body></html>"
// %%
// The library and the static Worker it calls, joined as the core joins them: the library is worker:brain-x-library there.
libraryRig = async () => {
  const stat = await simulate(static_service, {});
  const asked = [], cards = [], state = { down: false };
  const sim = await simulate(library_service, {
    config: { host: "brain.example" },
    core: async (request) => {
      const url = new URL(request.url);
      asked.push(url.pathname.split(".").pop() + " " + (url.searchParams.get("path") || ""));
      // knowledge.put as the core passes it on: the cards are kept for the test to read.
      if (url.pathname.endsWith("knowledge.put")) return state.down ? new Response("{}", { status: 503 }) : ((sent) => (cards.push(...sent), Response.json({ ids: sent.map((e) => e.id) })))((await request.json()).entries);
      return stat.fetch("https://static.internal" + url.pathname + url.search, {
        method: request.method,
        headers: { "content-type": request.headers.get("content-type") || "", "x-brain-caller": "worker:brain-x-library" },
        body: request.method === "GET" ? undefined : await request.arrayBuffer()
      });
    }
  });
  const call = (who, path, init = {}) => sim.fetch("https://library.internal" + path, { ...init, headers: { ...(init.headers || {}), "x-brain-caller": who } });
  const X = "/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.library.";
  const put = (who, name, html, extra = "") => call(who, X + "put?name=" + encodeURIComponent(name) + extra, { method: "POST", body: html });
  const post = (who, name, input) => call(who, X + name, { method: "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json" }, body: JSON.stringify(input) });
  return { stat, sim, asked, cards, state, call, put, post, X };
}
// %%
test_library_keeps_and_serves_a_notebook = {
  const rig = await libraryRig();
  const one = libraryNotebook("one");
  const made = await (await rig.put("owner", "notes", one)).json();
  expect(made).toMatchObject({ name: "notes", title: "Notes", sha256: await sha256(one), size: one.length, public: false, versions: 1 });
  // The file is in the static Worker's store, under library/, and not public there.
  const file = "library/notes/" + made.sha256.slice(0, 16) + ".html";
  expect([...rig.stat.blobs.keys()]).toEqual(["brain-x-static/f/" + file]);
  expect(rig.stat.rows.get("f/" + file)).toMatchObject({ public: false, type: "text/html; charset=utf-8" });
  const page = await rig.call("owner", "/library/notes");
  expect([page.status, page.headers.get("content-type"), page.headers.get("x-library-sha256"), await page.text()]).toEqual([200, "text/html; charset=utf-8", made.sha256, one]);
  expect((await rig.call("anonymous", "/library/notes")).status).toBe(401);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "/library/notes", { headers: { "if-none-match": '"' + made.sha256 + '"' } })).status).toBe(304);
  expect((await rig.call("owner", "/library/nothing")).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await rig.put("owner", "page", "<html><body>not a notebook</body></html>")).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.put("owner", "a/b", one)).status).toBe(400);
  return "put, served, 401, 304, 404, 400";
}
// %%
test_library_public_list_and_versions = {
  const rig = await libraryRig();
  const one = libraryNotebook("one"), two = libraryNotebook("two", "Notes, edited");
  const v1 = await (await rig.put("owner", "notes", one)).json();
  await rig.put("owner", "private", libraryNotebook("p", "Private"));
  const list = async (who) => (await (await rig.call(who, rig.X + "list")).json()).notebooks.map((n) => n.name + (n.public ? " public" : ""));
  expect(await list("anonymous")).toEqual([]);
  expect(await (await rig.post("owner", "setPublic", { name: "notes", public: true })).json()).toEqual({ name: "notes", public: true });
  expect(await list("anonymous")).toEqual(["notes public"]);
  expect(await list("owner")).toEqual(["notes public", "private"]);
  // A person granted library.list is anyone here: the public ones, and no notebook that is not.
  expect(await list("did:plc:friend")).toEqual(["notes public"]);
  expect((await rig.call("did:plc:friend", "/library/private")).status).toBe(401);
  expect(await list("token:laptop")).toEqual(["notes public", "private"]);
  // A second save: the name serves the new file, the old one by ?v=, and it stays public.
  expect((await rig.put("owner", "notes", two, "&parent=" + "0".repeat(64))).status).toBe(409);
  const v2 = await (await rig.put("owner", "notes", two, "&parent=" + v1.sha256)).json();
  expect(v2).toMatchObject({ title: "Notes, edited", public: true, versions: 2 });
  expect(await (await rig.call("anonymous", "/library/notes")).text()).toBe(two);
  expect(await (await rig.call("anonymous", "/library/notes?v=" + v1.sha256)).text()).toBe(one);
  expect((await rig.call("anonymous", "/library/notes?v=" + "0".repeat(64))).status).toBe(404);
  expect((await (await rig.call("owner", rig.X + "versions?name=notes")).json()).versions.map((v) => v.sha256)).toEqual([v2.sha256, v1.sha256]);
  // Deleting removes every version's file.
  expect(await (await rig.post("owner", "delete", { name: "notes" })).json()).toEqual({ deleted: true, versions: 2 });
  expect([...rig.stat.blobs.keys()].length).toBe(1);
  expect((await rig.call("anonymous", "/library/notes")).status).toBe(404);
  return "2 versions, 1 conflict, 2 files deleted";
}
// %%
// A module block as the exporter writes it, in both forms of its define calls.
libraryModule = (id, body) => "<scr" + `ipt id="${id}" \n  type="text/plain"\n  data-mime="application/javascript"\n>\n${body}\n</scr` + `ipt>`
// %%
test_library_enters_a_card_for_each_module = {
  const rig = await libraryRig();
  // Joined here, so that a reader of this module's own source does not take the fixture's import for one of its own.
  const imported = "mod" + "ule @fx/iac";
  const boxes = libraryModule("@fx/Boxes", 'const _a = function _anonymous(md) {return (md`# Leased boxes`)};\nconst _c = function _c(md) {return (md`## How\n\nRun code in a \\`linux\\` box.`)};\nconst _b = function _b(md) {return (md`## Tests`)};\nexport default function define(runtime, observer) {\n  $def("_a", null, ["md"], _a);\n  $def("_x", "boxPanel", ["htl"], _x);\n  $def("_v", "viewof size", [], _v);\n  $def("_s", "size", [], _s);\n  $def("_t", "test_boxes_run", [], _t);\n  main.define("' + imported + '", [], async () => 1);\n  main.define("rows", ["' + imported + '","@variable"], (_, v) => v.import("rows", _));\n}');
  const plain = libraryModule("@fx/plain", 'const _1 = function _1(md){return(\nmd`No heading here.`\n)};\nexport default function define(runtime, observer) {\n  const main = runtime.module();\n  main.variable(observer()).define(["md"], _1);\n  main.variable(observer("draw")).define("draw", [], _2);\n}');
  // A file attachment is not a module, whatever its name.
  const lib = "<scr" + 'ipt id="@fx/Boxes/lib.js.gz" type="text/plain" data-mime="application/gzip" data-encoding="base64">AAAA</scr' + 'ipt>';
  // Nor is a tag written in a page of prose, though what follows it reads like a module's block.
  const page = "<scr" + 'ipt id="@fx/wiki/page.md" type="text/plain" data-mime="text/markdown">kept as `<scr' + 'ipt id="@user/module-name" type="text/plain" data-mime="application/javascript">` blocks\n$def("_c", "css", [], _c)</scr' + "ipt>";
  const html = libraryNotebook(boxes + plain + lib + page);
  const made = await (await rig.put("owner", "fx", html)).json();
  expect([made.cards, rig.cards.length]).toEqual([2, 2]);
  expect(rig.cards[0]).toEqual({ id: "module:fx:boxes", kind: "module", title: "@fx/Boxes: Leased boxes", text: "Run code in a `linux` box.\nCells: boxPanel, size\nImports: @fx/iac", url: "https://brain.example/library/fx", source: "library", file: "library/fx/" + made.sha256.slice(0, 16) + ".html", method: "library.put", unlessPublic: true });
  expect(rig.cards[1]).toMatchObject({ id: "module:fx:plain", title: "@fx/plain", text: "No heading here.\nCells: draw" });
  // The cards of a public notebook are public; index enters them again from the kept file.
  await rig.post("owner", "setPublic", { name: "fx", public: true });
  expect(await (await rig.post("owner", "index", { name: "fx" })).json()).toEqual({ name: "fx", cards: 2 });
  expect([rig.cards.length, rig.cards[2].public, rig.cards[3].public, "unlessPublic" in rig.cards[2]]).toEqual([4, true, true, false]);
  // knowledge.put refuses: the notebook is kept, and the answer says no card was entered.
  rig.state.down = true;
  const again = await (await rig.put("owner", "fx", libraryNotebook(boxes, "Again"))).json();
  expect([again.cards, again.versions, again.title]).toEqual([0, 2, "Again"]);
  // A notebook with no module makes no call.
  const before = rig.asked.length;
  expect((await (await rig.put("owner", "notes", libraryNotebook("one"))).json()).cards).toBe(0);
  expect(rig.asked.slice(before).some((a) => a.startsWith("put ") && !a.includes("library/"))).toBe(false);
  expect((await rig.post("owner", "index", { name: "nothing" })).status).toBe(404);
  return "2 modules, 2 cards";
}
// %%
test_library_keeps_ten_versions = {
  const rig = await libraryRig();
  for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) await rig.put("owner", "notes", libraryNotebook("save " + i));
  const { versions } = await (await rig.call("owner", rig.X + "versions?name=notes")).json();
  expect(versions.length).toBe(10);
  expect([...rig.stat.blobs.keys()].length).toBe(10);
  expect(await (await rig.call("owner", "/library/notes")).text()).toBe(libraryNotebook("save 11"));
  expect(rig.asked.filter((a) => a.startsWith("delete")).length).toBe(2);
  return "12 saves, 10 kept";
}
// %%
test_library_declares_what_it_needs = {
  const { meta } = await library_service.emit();
  expect(meta).toMatchObject({
    worker: "brain-x-library", role: "recipe", module: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-library", resources: ["rows", "xrpc"], secrets: [],
    calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.knowledge.put", "com.lopecode.brain.static.delete", "com.lopecode.brain.static.get", "com.lopecode.brain.static.put"],
    paths: [{ path: "/library/*", who: "anyone" }]
  });
  expect(meta.access["com.lopecode.brain.library.put"]).toMatchObject({ allow: "caller.session", fixed: true });
  return meta.calls.join(", ");
}
// %%
test_library_panel_lists_notebooks = {
  const client = { query: async () => ({ notebooks: [{ name: "notes", title: "Notes", size: 4096, public: true, savedAt: 0, versions: 2 }] }) };
  const el = libraryPanel({ client, origin: "https://brain.example", owner: true });
  await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 0));
  expect(el.querySelector("a").getAttribute("href")).toBe("https://brain.example/library/notes");
  expect([...el.querySelectorAll("button")].map((b) => b.textContent)).toEqual(["Refresh", "Make public / owner only", "Delete", "Upload"]);
  expect(libraryPanel({ client: null }).textContent).toMatch(/Open this notebook from a Brain/);
  return "1 row, 4 buttons";
}
